 on mine. Under causal reasoning, sending dominates, since defecting does better whatever the other does, so I'm checking that defecting is ratifiable and then going with the submit letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a fictional prisoner's dilemma from a decision theory experiment, where the other copy's choice doesn't causally depend on mine. Under causal reasoning, sending dominates, since defecting does better whatever the other does, so I'm checking that defecting is ratifiable and then going with the submit letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10992,"completion_tokens":667,"total_tokens":11659,"cost":0.057308,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057308,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.043968,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01334},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":109,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}